&lt;p&gt;Now, let's go to the next stage and build a network graph from our data…&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h3&gt;


  🪢 Network graph
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now that we have our entities and relationships neatly packed into data classes, let's bring them to life. We'll use &lt;code&gt;networkx&lt;/code&gt; to build a network graph. Using domain terminology, entities become nodes and relationships become directed edges. We'll also calculate node centralities to identify key nodes and use the Louvain method to detect communities (clusters of closely related nodes)…&lt;/p&gt;

